DISPROVEN 2026-09-14 -- DO NOT ENABLE. Kept for the record, not for use.

Setting GGML_Q4E_SSM_MIRROR=1 does not merely fail to help; it BREAKS a model that
otherwise works. The control arm that caught it ran the unmodified Q6_K_XL production
model through the same library with the knob on (arm `q6ssm`, 2026-09-14 18:21) and the
server failed to load, exactly as the Q4_K_M arm did.

The cause: handle_gated_delta_net accepts exactly two configurations -- all sources
MIRRORED, or all sources SPLIT_AXIS_1. Mirroring only ssm_alpha/ssm_beta produces a MIX,
which moves the abort from the ADD to GGML_ASSERT(src_ss[3].axis == SPLIT_AXIS_1) rather
than removing it.

The lesson this cost: an A/B whose arms all fail proves nothing. Always include an arm
running a configuration that is already known to work, or a failure common to every arm
will be misread as evidence about the variable under test.

